WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.080
Speaker 1: Let's go next to J.C. from Brussels.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.940
J.C., welcome to the program.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:06.940
Hi.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.809
Can you hear me?

00:00:08.809 --> 00:00:10.530
Yes, I can.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.249
Speaker 6: Okay.

00:00:12.249 --> 00:00:13.249
Did you hear that?

00:00:13.249 --> 00:00:20.050
Last year, this data company called Morning
Consult did a survey in a number of Western

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:26.220
countries to see how much of the population
had what they call the authoritarian personality.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.220
Hmm.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.220
Have you were you.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.220
Have you heard of this?

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:30.220
Speaker 1: Yes, I have.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.040
I don't remember what the results were, but
I remember the survey.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.810
Speaker 6: Yes.

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:41.440
It turns out that about 26% of Americans have
highly authoritarian personalities.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.410
Speaker 1: Sounds about right.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:47.650
Speaker 6: Whereas only 6.7% of Germans do.

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:48.760
Speaker 1: Hmm.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:49.760
That's interesting.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:51.880
Speaker 6: That's quite a historical irony.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:58.690
I mean, Germany used to be the land of the
Nazis, but now they are the most liberal country

00:00:58.690 --> 00:00:59.730
in the Western Hemisphere.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.170
Speaker 1: Is that true?

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:02.170
Judged.

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:03.170
Judged how?

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:04.870
Speaker 6: Yes.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:10.580
If you go to the Wikipedia article for the
authoritarian personality, all the data is

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:11.950
there.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:18.310
And in most of the European countries, only
10% or so of the population is highly authoritarian.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:22.100
Speaker 1: Ah, because there is other ways
to evaluate it.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:29.020
Like I found another study here which has
Germany ninth in most left wing and it says

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:37.440
the most left wing countries are Norway, Sweden,
Denmark, Finland, Iceland, New Zealand, Switzerland,

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:38.909
Canada, then Germany.

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:44.671
Now I think the difference is you're talking
about a survey, I think, of the people, whereas

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:48.700
this might be a survey more of of what is
government policy.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:50.950
Speaker 6: Wow.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:51.950
Okay.

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:54.970
Yeah, there was just eight countries in that
survey.

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:58.460
To the north, Scandinavia was not part of
it.

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:00.560
Speaker 1: Oh, they didn't even include it.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:01.560
Well, that doesn't.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:06.470
If you're talking about the West, I think
you must include Scandinavia, don't you think?

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:09.030
Speaker 6: Yeah, but I see they only did eight
countries.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.030
Okay.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:12.230
But I think it still is.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:13.230
But you're right.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.230
Canada is pretty.

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:15.230
Speaker 1: Liberal.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:16.230
Yeah.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:19.480
I mean, when there's almost 200 countries
to only look at eight and say Germany's the

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.750
most liberal seems a little narrow.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.230
Speaker 6: Yes.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:24.230
True.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:27.200
Still, it's pretty scary how authoritarian
America is.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.200
Speaker 1: Oh, it's horrible.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:32.730
Speaker 6: American Americans like to think
of themselves as the great freedom loving

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:33.730
people.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:35.480
But yeah, the data, they're not.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.940
They're the most authoritarian people in the
developed world.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:44.030
Speaker 1: Yeah, well, the American right
is all about the freedom to live however you

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.610
want, as long as it's okay with them.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:48.060
Speaker 2: Trust.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.510
Speaker 6: Yeah.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:50.510
Conformism.

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:51.510
Speaker 2: Right.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:53.920
Speaker 1: Well, J.C., thank you for the call.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:55.490
How how's Brussels these days?

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:57.660
One of my favorite cities in the world.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.590
Speaker 6: Oh, yeah.

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:00.660
The weather's nice.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.660
Right.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:02.739
We got.

00:03:02.739 --> 00:03:04.670
We got spared the worst of the heat wave.

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:05.670
Speaker 1: Nice.

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:06.670
Good.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:08.099
Well, I hope to get back there sooner than
later.

00:03:08.099 --> 00:03:09.379
Speaker 6: Okay.

00:03:09.379 --> 00:03:10.379
See?

00:03:10.379 --> 00:03:15.541
Speaker 1: All right, J.C., not that excited
for my triumphant return to Belgium, but that's

00:03:15.541 --> 00:03:16.590
okay.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:16.940
That's okay

